{"status": "progress", "message": "Retrieved 130 candidate paragraphs; kept 3", "stage": "retrieve", "claim_index": 2, "data": {"kind": "retrieval", "pass": 1, "queries": ["James Webb Space Telescope", "Lagrangian point"], "candidates": 130, "by_source": {"web": 3, "wikipedia": 127}, "avgdl": 115.9, "top": [{"text": "May 19, 2021 \u00b7 The James Webb Space Telescope orbits the Sun near Sun-Earth Lagrange point 2 (L2), approximately 1.5 million kilometers (1 million miles) from E", "source": "web", "dense": 0.816, "bm25": 16.65, "dense_rank": 2, "bm25_rank": 1, "rrf": 0.03252, "selected": true}, {"text": "Apr 30, 2025 \u00b7 A Solar Orbit The James Webb Space Telescope is not in orbit around the Earth, like the Hubble Space Telescope is - it actually orbits the Sun, 1", "source": "web", "dense": 0.831, "bm25": 16.15, "dense_rank": 1, "bm25_rank": 2, "rrf": 0.03252, "selected": true}, {"text": "Several planets have trojan asteroids near their L4 and L5 points with respect to the Sun; Jupiter has more than one million of these trojans. Some Lagrange poi", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.663, "bm25": 11.44, "dense_rank": 6, "bm25_rank": 3, "rrf": 0.03102, "selected": true}, {"text": "The Deep Space Climate Observatory (DSCOVR), an artificial satellite, is located at L1 to study solar wind coming toward Earth from the Sun and to monitor Earth", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.648, "bm25": 10.02, "dense_rank": 7, "bm25_rank": 5, "rrf": 0.03031, "selected": false}, {"text": "Orbit On 22 January 2022, Webb successfully completed a final correction burn that placed it into its desired orbit, roughly 1.5 million kilometers away from th", "source": "web", "dense": 0.683, "bm25": 9.0, "dense_rank": 3, "bm25_rank": 12, "rrf": 0.02976, "selected": false}, {"text": "In January 2022, it arrived at its destination, a solar orbit near the Sun\u2013Earth L2 Lagrange point, about 1.5 million kilometers (930,000 mi) from Earth. The te", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.664, "bm25"